# NexaFlow — SELinux policy snippet (optional, usually not needed)
# Place under device/<oem>/<codename>/sepolicy/vendor/ or system/sepolicy
# only if your Evolution X device tree denies priv-app access to settings provider.
#
# Most Evolution X trees already allow priv-apps to write Settings.Secure /
# Settings.System via the `priv_app` domain. This file is a no-op placeholder
# that documents the minimal allowances NexaFlow would need if your tree strips them.
#
# type nexaflow_app, domain;
# app_domain(nexaflow_app)
# priv_app_domain(nexaflow_app)
# allow nexaflow_app settings_provider:dir search;
# allow nexaflow_app settings_provider:file { read write open };
